# Build context for every image is the repository ROOT, not the workspace:
#
#   docker build -f infra/docker/api-gateway.Dockerfile .
#
# The repository has one lockfile, at the root, and installs through npm
# workspaces, so an image can only run `npm ci` from here.
#
# One file serves all FOUR Dockerfiles in infra/docker — api-gateway,
# core-service, module-service and nextjs — so it is the union of what they
# need, not the intersection. The backend images take apps/api, the module
# backends and every workspace's package.json; nextjs.Dockerfile additionally
# takes apps/web, modules/*/frontend and packages/, because a Next workspace
# imports from packages/shared-core and the shell imports from the module
# zones. Excluding those three (as this file did while no image built a Next
# app) turned the Next build into a missing-module failure, so anything added
# here has to be weighed against that image too.

# The image runs `npm ci` itself; a host node_modules is dead weight and risks
# baking host-built native modules into the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — the image builds its own.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
*.tsbuildinfo

# Never copy real credentials into a layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Tests are not built or shipped.
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.e2e-spec.ts
**/__tests__
coverage
**/coverage

# Tooling no image touches. apps/web, modules/*/frontend and packages/ used to
# be excluded here and are not any more: nextjs.Dockerfile builds from them.
# The backend images still only COPY the paths they name, so the cost is upload
# size, not layer size.
apps/mcp-server
docs
# Cross-service test assets (Postman, smoke) are never part of an image.
tests
infra/k8s
skills
.claude
.github

# Local noise
.git
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.vscode
.idea
